G FOR?\n\nThis opportunity is designed for a **builder**.\n\nSomeone who can walk the plant floor in the morning, work through production and capacity issues with the team, and sit down with the President later that day to discuss capital, performance, strategy, and growth.\n\nYou'll likely bring:\n\n✔️ 15+ years of progressive manufacturing/operations leadership\n\n✔️ Experience building, launching, relocating, or significantly expanding a manufacturing operation\n\n✔️ Strong experience in **sheet metal fabrication, metal fabrication, welding, industrial equipment, HVAC/ductwork, process equipment, or engineered products**\n\n✔️ Experience recruiting and building both salaried and hourly teams\n\n✔️ A practical command of lean manufacturing, production planning, quality systems, constraint management, and continuous improvement\n\n✔️ The ability to lead with **high standards, low ego, and genuine respect for people**\n\nWHY THIS ROLE?\n\nBecause opportunities to truly **build something from the ground up** don't come along very often.\n\nIf you've spent your career thinking, “If I could build the operation myself, I'd do this differently…”\n\n**This may be your opportunity to do exactly that.**\n\n������ **Temple, Texas**\n\n������ High-mix custom manufacturing\n\n������ Significant long-term growth potential\n\n������ Competitive executive compensation + performance-based incentive opportunity + comprehensive benefits\n\nYou should be proficient in:\n\n* Leadership / People Management\n* Industrial and Manufacturing Engineering\n* Continuous Improvement\n* Manufacturing Instruction (MI)\n* Supervisory Experience\n* Glass Fabrication\n* Coaching and Mentoring Experience\n* Operational Risk Management\n* Workplace Safety & EHS Management\n* Metal Casting Experience","textSha256":"6ace27eec75fc69e301b45da37f01613f0cf1656e4263d999d9115015cf1dfe5","fullPosting":true,"facts":{"degree":{"text":"NOT_STATED","req":"NOT_STATED"},"pay":null,"payAmbiguous":false},"canonicalWr